    "title": "The Chords A Minor Gives You",
    "summary": "Harmonising A natural minor gives seven chords, three minor, three major, one diminished, and every root is already on your low E and A strings.",
    "tags": ["caged", "minor"],
    "readingTimeMin": 4,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take each note of "
        },
        {
          "text": "A B C D E F G",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " in turn. On each one, stack a third and a fifth, using only those seven notes — no note from outside the scale is allowed in. Seven chords fall out the other end, and no choices were made along the way. The scale did all of it."
        }
